4.
A Zomato user places an order. The probability they order Pizza is 0.3, and the probability they order Burger is 0.4. If the
probability they order both is 0.1, use the addition rule to find the probability the user orders Pizza or Burger.
<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A and B)</em>

probability of pizza P(A) = 0.3
probability of burger P(B)= 0.4
probability of both P(A and B)= 0.1

probability the user orders Pizza or Burger:
 
P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - p(A and B)
          = 0.3 + 0.4 - 0.1
          = 0.6
percentage = 0.6*100  = 60%

interpretation = The probability that a Zomato user orders either Pizza or Burger is 0.6 or 60%. This means there is a 60% chance that the
user will order Pizza, Burger, or both.

